{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01HYzpBKwKYdL5mNSTrGr4Rp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to determine what tasks to propose.\n\n## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nThe project is `go-unix-utils` - a specification-driven pipeline for reimplementing Unix utilities in Go. The pipeline:\n1. Extracts specs from C source\n2. Generates Go implementations from PRDs\n3. Verifies via differential testing\n\n## Step 2: Summarize Project State\n\n**Current state:**\n- Several utilities have specs written and code generated (at generation-merged tags): pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/wc, cmd/cat, cmd/sponge\n- Current branch (generation-gh-262-codegen) is clean with no code files\n\n\n- Issue #291 tracks the format package work for column alignment, ANSI color, and size formatting, which is ready to implement\n\n## Step 3: Reason About Priorities\n\nGiven the release constraint limiting me to version 00.0 use cases, I'm checking which ones are in scope: the magefiles use case hasn't started yet, while the format package is already implemented but hasn't had code generation started.\n\nLooking at the spec statuses, I notice issue #291 already covers the format package implementation, so I shouldn't duplicate that work. The other use cases I should consider are the magefiles and sys packages, both of which are spec-complete but haven't begun coding yet.\n\nFor the magefiles use case, the actual generation target is `cmd/version/` rather than the magefiles directory itself, since the scaffolding is handled separately. I'm also noticing a discrepancy where testutils appears in the rel01.0 roadmap but was already released in rel00.0 based on the implementation status.\n\nNow I'm cross-referencing the implementation status with the roadmap and seeing some inconsistencies—pkg/format shows as \"spec implemented, code not started\" in the road