 the verification harness that every downstream utility depends on for its differential tests, making it the highest-value first step. The DiffTest struct is a single bounded type with exactly 4 capabilities from the architecture, fitting the 4-requirement constraint precisely. Proposing `pkg/testutils` first.\n\n## Step 4: Propose Task\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/testutils DiffTest struct and Run harness (rel00.0-uc004)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component section and DiffTest data structure entry under interfaces.data_structures)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml (concrete execution flow for the harness)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (full requirements; if this path does not resolve, use Glob with pattern docs/specs/product-requirements/prd*-testutils.yaml to find the correct file)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, normalization hook type, and Run method\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define DiffTest struct with exported fields for reference binary path, subject binary path, args ([]string), stdin content ([]byte), environment variables ([]string), expected exit code (int), expected stdout ([]byte), and expected stderr ([]byte) -- per prd001-testutils R1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement Run(t *testing.T) method that executes both the reference binary and the subject binary with identical args, stdin, and environment via os/exec, capturing stdout, stderr, and exit code for each run -- per prd001-testutils R2\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Compare captured stdout, stderr, and exit code between the reference run and the subject run; call t.Errorf for each divergence, including the args used, the reference value, and the subject value in the error message -- per prd001-testutils R3\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Support optional normalization hook fields on DiffTest (function types that transform []byte output before comparison) so callers can mask acceptable differences such as timestamps before the byte-for-byte comparison -- per prd001-testutils R4\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"The primary exported type is DiffTest; the source file must be named difftest.go, not testutils.go -- the package is named testutils matching the directory, per architecture naming conventions (P7: file named after primary exported type)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"pkg/testutils uses only the Go standard library (os/exec, bytes, strings, testing, os); do not import golang.org/x/sys or any external package -- the harness needs no platform-specific syscalls\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Module path is github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils; the package declaration in difftest.go is 'package testutils'\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/testutils/difftest.go compiles without errors under go build ./pkg/testutils/...\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"DiffTest struct has exported fields for both binary paths, args, stdin, env, expected exit code, expected stdout, and expected stderr\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Run method executes both binaries and calls t.Errorf with a descriptive message (including args and differing values) when stdout, stderr, or exit code diverges between reference and subject\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"DiffTest has at least one normalization hook field of function type; the hook is applied to captured output before comparison when the field is non-nil\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"golangci-lint passes on pkg/testutils/difftest.go with no warnings under the project's standard linting configuration\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"d84e6bc8-fd06-4a9c-82e3-14d604e19fcc","total_cost_usd":0.5319295,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_c